<!--
    kuna `linearswitch N`: loweredswitch re-rolls only a binary-search
    compare cascade, because a linear chain of equality tests reads as a
    hand-written if/else.  With `linearswitch 3` a linear chain of at least
    three cases on one variable re-rolls too, when every case body is entered
    only from the chain and the head dominates it (a chain the compiler copied
    into two paths keeps its ifs), and its labels print the same signed or
    unsigned.  Default off: re-rolling moves datatest assertions.

    Stage / sub-stage: P2 "switch-model", option `linearswitch off|N`.

    The bytes are decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/linearswitch.c
    built by clang 22.1 -O2 -fno-pie -no-pie -nostartfiles (x86-64): sw3 (a
    three-case switch clang lowers to a linear chain) and chain (an
    if/else-if chain on one variable).  Pass 1 is the default (off), pass 2 sets
    `linearswitch 3`.
-->
